<div class="detail-grid"><div class="detail-main"><section class="panel"><div class="panel-header"><div><h3>Calculation</h3><p>The strongest normalization supported by the attached evidence.</p></div></div><div class="panel-body">{formula}<dl class="definition-grid" style="margin-top:14px"><div class="definition"><dt>Recurring price</dt><dd>{e(plan['priceDisplay'])}</dd></div><div class="definition"><dt>Quantified value</dt><dd>{e(plan['valueDisplay'])}</dd></div><div class="definition"><dt>Value represented</dt><dd>{e(represented)}</dd></div><div class="definition"><dt>Usage unit</dt><dd>{e(plan.get('unit') or 'Undisclosed')}</dd></div><div class="definition"><dt>Eligibility</dt><dd>{e(plan.get('eligibility'))}</dd></div><div class="definition"><dt>Benchmark coverage</dt><dd>{e(plan.get('benchmarkCoverage'))}</dd></div><div class="definition"><dt>Last verified</dt><dd>{e(plan.get('lastVerified'))}</dd></div></dl></div></section>{unknown_panel}{quota_panel}{details_panel}{model_panel}{task_panel}{benchmark_panel}</div><aside class="detail-aside">{notes_panel}{tag_panel}<section class="panel"><div class="panel-header"><h3>Evidence</h3></div><div class="panel-body source-list">{source_links or '<p class="cell-sub">No attached source record yet.</p>'}</div></section><a class="button" href="/plans/">← Back to all plans</a></aside></div>'''
        write_page(f"/plans/{plan['id']}/", layout(f"{plan['provider']} {plan['name']}", body, f"/plans/{plan['id']}/", plan["headline"]))


def build_benchmarks() -> None:
    agent_rows = sorted([b for b in benchmarks if b.get("benchmark") == "Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index"], key=lambda b: b["score"], reverse=True)
    model_rows = sorted([b for b in benchmarks if b.get("kind") == "model-intelligence"], key=lambda b: b["score"], reverse=True)
    terminal_rows = sorted([b for b in benchmarks if b.get("benchmark") == "Terminal-Bench"], key=lambda b: b["score"], reverse=True)
    agents = sorted({row["agent"] for row in agent_rows})
    options = "".join(f'<option value="{e(agent)}">{e(agent)}</option>' for agent in agents)
    agent_html = "".join(f'''<tr data-benchmark-row data-agent="{e(row['agent'])}" data-search="{e((row['agent']+' '+row['model']).lower())}"><td><strong>{e(row['agent'])}</strong><span class="cell-sub">{e(row['model'])}</span></td><td class="numeric">{fmt(row['score'])}</td><td class="numeric">{'$'+fmt(row.get('apiCostPerTaskUsd'),2) if row.get('apiCostPerTaskUsd') is not None else '—'}</td><td class="numeric">{'$'+fmt(row.get('apiUsdPerExpectedPass'),3) if row.get('apiUsdPerExpectedPass') is not None else '—'}</td><td class="numeric">{fmt(row.get('expectedPassesPerApiDollar'),3)}</td><td class="numeric">{fmt(row.get('timePerTaskMinutes'),1)+'m' if row.get('timePerTaskMinutes') is not None else '—'}</td><td class="numeric">{fmt(row.get('minutesPerExpectedPass'),1)+'m' if row.get('minutesPerExpectedPass') is not None else '—'}</td><td>{'<span class="pareto-chip">cost</span>' if row.get('costQualityPareto') else ''} {'<span class="pareto-chip">time</span>' if row.get('timeQualityPareto') else ''} {'<span class="pareto-chip">tokens</span>' if row.get('tokenQualityPareto') else ''}</td></tr>''' for row in agent_rows)
    model_html = "".join(f'''<tr><td><strong>{e(row['model'])}</strong><span class="cell-sub">{e(row['provider'])}</span></td><td class="numeric">{fmt(row['score'])}</td><td class="numeric">${fmt(row.get('inputPricePerMUsd'),3)}</td><td class="numeric">${fmt(row.get('cachedInputPricePerMUsd'),3)}</td><td class="numeric">${fmt(row.get('outputPricePerMUsd'),3)}</td><td class="numeric">${fmt(row.get('blendedPricePerMUsd'),3)}</td><td class="numeric">${fmt(row.get('blendedUsdPerIntelligencePoint'),5)}</td><td class="numeric">{fmt(row.get('outputTokensPerSecond'),1)+' t/s' if row.get('outputTokensPerSecond') is not None else '—'}</td><td>{'<span class="pareto-chip">price</span>' if row.get('priceIntelligencePareto') else ''} {'<span class="pareto-chip">speed</span>' if row.get('speedIntelligencePareto') else ''}</td></tr>''' for row in model_rows)
    terminal_cards = "".join(insight_card(f"{row['score']}%", row["agent"], row["model"]) for row in terminal_rows)
    body = f'''<section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">External results only</p><h1>Quality remains attached to the tested model, harness, and benchmark.</h1><p class="lede">The dashboard imports publisher-owned values and derives transparent ratios from them. It does not run a private suite, infer scores for untested subscription routes, or treat an Intelligence Index as a task pass rate.</p></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="callout"><strong>Cost per expected pass is available only for pass-rate-like coding-agent scores.</strong> It equals API cost per task divided by score/100; failed attempts remain in the economics. Model Intelligence Index rows instead use blended dollars per million tokens per intelligence point.</div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="toolbar"><div class="control"><label for="benchmark-search">Search benchmark rows</label><input id="benchmark-search" data-benchmark-search type="search" placeholder="Agent or model…"></div><div class="control"><label for="benchmark-agent">Agent</label><select id="benchmark-agent" data-benchmark-agent><option value="all">All agents</option>{options}</select></div></div><div class="panel"><div class="table-shell"><table data-benchmark-table><thead><tr><th>Agent / model</th><th>Index</th><th>API cost/task</th><th>API $/expected pass</th><th>Passes/API $</th><th>Time/task</th><th>Minutes/expected pass</th><th>Pareto</th></tr></thead><tbody>{agent_html}</tbody></table></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">Model-level evidence</p><h2>Intelligence, blended price, and speed</h2></div><p>The 7:2:1 blended price weights cache reads, fresh input, and output according to Artificial Analysis's published convention.</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="table-shell"><table><thead><tr><th>Provider / model</th><th>Intelligence</th><th>Input/M</th><th>Cache/M</th><th>Output/M</th><th>7:2:1 blended/M</th><th>$/M/intelligence point</th><th>Speed</th><th>Pareto</th></tr></thead><tbody>{model_html}</tbody></table></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">Separate benchmark</p><h2>Terminal-Bench 2.1</h2></div><p>These pass rates are retained separately from the Coding Agent Index and model Intelligence Index.</p></div><div class="insight-grid">{terminal_cards}</div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="callout warning"><strong>Plan transfer requires evidence.</strong> A model result can inform a plan's quality signal when the checkpoint matches, but native-agent task-capacity calculations are published only when the tested harness and a quantified subscription denominator can be joined directly.</div></section>'''
